{
  "$schema_notes": [
    "Domain taxonomy consumed by scripts/generate_skills_summary.py.",
    "",
    "Why this file exists rather than a `domain:` key in each SKILL.md:",
    "the frontmatter field is declared by only ~half the skills and uses 21",
    "inconsistent values (23 of them are just 'genomics'), so it cannot",
    "produce a balanced taxonomy. Keeping the mapping in one reviewable file",
    "also makes reclassification a single-file diff.",
    "",
    "Membership keys are CLI aliases for registered skills and folder names",
    "for agent-readable ones. Those two namespaces do not currently overlap;",
    "the generator asserts that and fails if it ever changes.",
    "",
    "Every skill must appear in exactly one domain. The generator exits",
    "non-zero listing any skill that is unclassified or unknown, so adding a",
    "skill without classifying it is a hard failure rather than a silent",
    "omission from the report."
  ],
